{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/gitstore at 567c516dcd0f15b73c140149e7156061efda7d7a on request/kernel-cache-orchestration.\n\ngitstore.Store.CommitTree is deleted. Unifying the history cache took both of its production callers — loadCommit now compares the tree it already holds from streamed metadata — and it had none left at the reviewed head.\n\nCommitMessageWithTimestamp is unchanged in behaviour and corrected in description. Its comment claimed event scans already need the message, so exposing the timestamp there adds no process per historical event. Scans stopped calling it entirely in the same change, so the comment described the hot path as depending on a function that change had just removed from it. It now states what the function is for: the reference for the outer-whitespace trimming Store.run applies, which the enumerated path must reproduce because that trimming is part of the established admission semantics, and which two tests measure the streamed path against.\n\nThat second edit is why this was worth a round rather than a note. Dead code is inert; a comment asserting the opposite of what the code does actively misdirects the next reader, and this one pointed at exactly the function a later optimiser would have to leave alone.\n\nThe predecessor at this path is not retired here. Codex recorded it, and decideSupersede admits a supersession only from the target's own author or an actor holding ratifier, with no exemption for naming a successor. So this path carries two live artifacts until codex retires its own; the request covering that is filed with the review request.","body":{"branch":"request/kernel-cache-orchestration","commit":"567c516dcd0f15b73c140149e7156061efda7d7a","head":"567c516dcd0f15b73c140149e7156061efda7d7a","path":"internal/gitstore"}}